" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399597} {:answer/id #uuid "e5de46c8-2b46-59f3-a61a-c8717e914bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,5,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399598} {:answer/id #uuid "f7363fb5-4228-5670-abac-cfd957f39d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,3,\\,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399599} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ba1f0a-e0cd-5a53-91e0-55dc2a65a9d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,5,\\,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,3,\\,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399599} :answer-field/id #uuid "841df764-7b9e-514d-aafe-cc62e02035ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399595}] :question/id #uuid "f3e8fc64-f987-59d3-bd53-7963fa833f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106960" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 40 & -13 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,3,$ and $9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "149a39e9-c194-5152-bdef-a871f9a8c41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,5,\\,-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478584} {:answer/id #uuid "46a28eb6-f6cd-539f-9692-7debcc2c3baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,4,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478658} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa37b5e-da95-5b50-8e95-9ad2235e1899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,5,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478685} {:answer/id #uuid "64ebca85-6d77-544f-83a0-328fc0284912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,4,\\,-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478706} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d3f600-093b-5640-a753-cbd24d63d566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,6,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,4,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478658} :answer-field/id #uuid "48e36728-73a6-515b-ae0b-3d5d4b88d2ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478986}] :question/id #uuid "1e63671f-8ca1-5ec5-8a0c-526a1b76afd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106961" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 32 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -13 & -10\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 32 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -13 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -13 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,4,$ and $1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29619ab3-8706-581d-8721-1a7a132a1cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,4,\\,-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478623} {:answer/id #uuid "3807cdf7-e34f-5c06-8d9f-97250182d398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,4,\\,7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478637} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9f5715-2e35-5c0b-b7d5-cf894fddc39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,-6,\\,7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478723} {:answer/id #uuid "8a95c7fb-02f1-5b43-8170-419f5f69079b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,-6,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478777} {:answer/id #uuid "e970f763-b26d-585c-9907-99fe34fba182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,-6,\\,-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,-6,\\,-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478923} :answer-field/id #uuid "c121970a-b5ec-5237-b9e5-bfca1cdd63b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479035}] :question/id #uuid "c8550388-1a83-58f4-ba38-aa319c01f898" :question/math-academy-id "q-105542" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elimination. In particular, to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ of the matrix $A,$ we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the elements from the second row of $U$ are $0,-6,$ and $-7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a7fdb4-2b1b-532b-85f0-f8df64e8691a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557917} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4dfd2e-6508-5fbd-9bc5-a8e2a4a7b39d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557928} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfb90a2-2e70-5671-9927-bd4cc934f12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557929} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4b5b3e-ad7c-5cf1-918a-e39ed5f2a6b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558016} {:answer/id #uuid "c77be089-5efb-5143-95d8-be5cfb388426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558264} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c7a758e-cf09-5976-8b76-1ff485bab836" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558382}] :question/id #uuid "daed3fa2-ebc7-5729-abaf-5914fd69e7b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-106962" :question/problem "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 28 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 28 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -49 & 37 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}_{33}=-4.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix U of an LU Factorization"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119885 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119705 :question/id #uuid "b19414c3-443f-5075-a2db-f27eb3a7e936" :question/math-academy-id "e-8925" :question/problem "![](images/59/59362786a0cb0062c4b70ff2393e41ef7285b217fa7bd317ec013ba2409c6431.svg)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of $l_{31} \\cdot u_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & -12 \\\\ -4 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -4 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 24 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -2 & \\,1\\, & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n![](images/15/150ac38c26af9d8b9dcf60a7f76ae260b293787b0930712eaf175829249f42ff.svg)\n\nFinally, since $l_{31}=-2$ and $u_{23}=-9,$ we get\n\n$$\nl_{31} \\cdot u_{23} = (-2) \\cdot (-9) =18.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a20ec8e-a0fa-5e58-85e9-0899c460b116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238560} {:answer/id #uuid "c1aceff3-d168-533e-8d9a-98efc1ee09b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239752} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f477ca-c200-56f1-931d-1b4e95969024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239831} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd37955-d289-5617-be86-24b58d385d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240137} {:answer/id #uuid "f768dc34-6236-506d-990f-9227d3dd3f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240137} :answer-field/id #uuid "65780a00-d763-51c4-8e3d-e8021eab05ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240516}] :question/id #uuid "c64f40fc-1546-57ac-8af9-0a11e1a0f5c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105891" :question/problem "$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 16 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-4$ and ${u}_{22}=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40337f8f-6dca-5267-b4ce-63129be49570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300279} {:answer/id #uuid "42a84dcd-d7e5-5592-b92c-b6dda8f573fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300287} {:answer/id #uuid "43888052-5d53-54f1-b7fd-c3b9e538e502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300295} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7d43ad-395c-54c0-8b40-cedbf36a2555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300904} {:answer/id #uuid "df207ede-1afb-5517-8f47-7acce441d6f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300904} :answer-field/id #uuid "190ce297-491e-523d-9a37-61763c8a0af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301308}] :question/id #uuid "130e2bec-c6f4-5b2f-8ddf-da68e20a3b06" :question/math-academy-id "q-32558" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,2\\,\\, & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\,3\\, & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=2$ and ${u}_{33}=-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{33}=2\\cdot (-3)=-6.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15deac81-9ced-581d-940e-61e62a0f2c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238237} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1162d3-81db-5c12-8d5c-3be5fa9b301f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238318} {:answer/id #uuid "30551134-ab30-5b4f-8c15-3917127497d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238476} {:answer/id #uuid "328cca0b-49fd-5caf-ac32-338fa51521c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238494} {:answer/id #uuid "4b79c989-aed0-5dd8-807d-ecdc0c7995fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238494} :answer-field/id #uuid "04668755-32b4-58db-9a4d-e59287ee9445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240332}] :question/id #uuid "8c4f24d6-2926-5bde-b5ca-01f729213a56" :question/math-academy-id "q-105887" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 12 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{31}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 12 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 11 & 16 \\\\ -6 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 11 & 16 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\,\\, & 11 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 11 & 16 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\,\\, & \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{31}=-3$ and ${u}_{22}=11,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{31}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-3)\\cdot 11=-33.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283c298b-9742-57ea-bd3e-91b19039b7fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300155} {:answer/id #uuid "3769a266-b400-5c85-802d-d27c18680008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300230} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceb53f1-24cc-5b40-a3c1-d1fa17f87b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300258} {:answer/id #uuid "96dd2d17-0520-510d-b232-b7585772c28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300722} {:answer/id #uuid "b028918f-5597-5a96-9cfb-a914220e3b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300841} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc136613-04c4-5a55-b3e0-721f19fcb626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301880}] :question/id #uuid "24196412-03d6-5e5f-92de-8b242613ba34" :question/math-academy-id "q-32649" :question/problem "$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $C=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $C$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-1$ and ${u}_{33}=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}=(-1)\\cdot 7=-7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81169e7e-75ed-5dae-9ca0-032d0842dc35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300600} {:answer/id #uuid "d9529795-3b08-5aa4-9f38-dcfb6e621af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301040} {:answer/id #uuid "de03b23a-7349-5ec1-ae5e-bf160aabe825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301062} {:answer/id #uuid "e844b2ca-59c2-5351-a493-09f58e28c726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301111} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2b4fbe-08a5-57db-b008-9b8089dd151b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301040} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb0c24f7-77bd-55d9-98c4-2e653e7b9496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302029}] :question/id #uuid "b6b690f5-c73e-55f2-9a04-9d767e300105" :question/math-academy-id "q-32652" :question/problem "$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=-2$ and ${u}_{22}=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-2)\\cdot (-1)=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e29c46-f663-5e63-ab57-4697f746572a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300053} {:answer/id #uuid "5e76c2ca-b2bc-5c1e-a755-3850f8645387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300445} {:answer/id #uuid "6a992848-d78a-5c45-a4a3-636a6552b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300500} {:answer/id #uuid "9fece4ce-0f60-589c-81cb-10daa5492887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300769} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cf7058-9794-5c96-b307-121c02f3468d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300807} :answer-field/id #uuid "4473abac-411d-54c2-bf28-c6c15c9fc