eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\sqrt{2},$ a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ is a vector $v$ such that \n\n$$\n(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}v=0\\,\\text{and}\\,(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}v\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nNotice the following:\n\n- We are given that $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}$ has dimension $2.$ This means that the solutions to $(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}v=0$ form a subspace of dimension $2.$\n\n- We are given that $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}$ has dimension $4.$ This means that the solutions to $(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}v=0$ form a subspace of dimension $4.$\n\nNow, since $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}$ is a subspace of dimension $2$ in $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}$, which is a subspace of dimension $4,$ our basis can contain only $2$ vectors that lie in $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}$ but does not lie in $\\text{Null}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, there will be \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{3}-\\text{nullity}(C-\\sqrt{2}I)^{2}=4-2=2\n$$\n\n generalized eigenvectors of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\sqrt{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c4a71d-0628-5ff8-8f7b-d46974a371a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490583} {:answer/id #uuid "4a251038-f751-5a21-aad4-7863df5e48fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490652} {:answer/id #uuid "6b88a4da-cde6-54e9-abf5-e9ffa5b03287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490719} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee85073-8e29-5a00-b49d-ca1b9acce08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490763} {:answer/id #uuid "966b8de0-1dc1-520c-ae6b-f1958e5ed590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490763} :answer-field/id 