86393734} {:answer/id #uuid "a11cb66a-4f2f-57d3-89e5-a6bf45c90fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3+8\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393735} {:answer/id #uuid "577953b3-72bf-57d8-ab26-324d137ae17c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393736} :answer-field/id #uuid "28dc495a-a187-507f-a135-8dc96fead918" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393731}] :question/id #uuid "711300c3-0b93-5c10-812e-3a69e9246478" :question/math-academy-id "q-77547" :question/problem "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ \\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152168 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151959 :question/id #uuid "a2c8f19f-6c69-5891-847e-b6ef26f657bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6560" :question/problem "If ![](images/e4/e482e62cbd229d5d7d86010ab39fea9c56ba4b1dc7bd0553cbfbb6a2fbfc8398.png) and ![](images/f4/f4542dad2dfcb51cd14caff63d99064d8a8e98772a58d4ab4022d2b572a1aad9.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the vector ![](images/8e/8e644a1eabc085ec8e7087e07d0e5860ebf1808a63747d4f9196e08b08dd72ce.png) what is the value of $ab+cd?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector ![](images/17/1751b58c55d6a2d44458a084d8beb31862afb4746645f10cfa04198a583f509e.png) we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3+7\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=-3, b=5, c=7$ and $d=-2,$ which implies that\n\n$$\nab+cd=(-3) \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot (-2) = -29.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0905dc61-4680-5cd7-8690-9a8726f0cd9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324053} {:answer/id #uuid "31c919de-2ba7-506d-b8bc-b68fe3f9583f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324376} {:answer/id #uuid "4b69368a-9de7-52e3-9e32-0034ce94f02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324585} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f0c75c-cb04-5875-92eb-d0fc785f9282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325656} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9b6136-5b10-59e5-b681-39ccee598e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324376} :answer-field/id #uuid "57a4b721-055a-525e-9216-35044caf1163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326370}] :question/id #uuid "0f76aac6-fb1f-5af4-a2f0-ac47a47590be" :question/math-academy-id "q-38388" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+bc?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=2,b=5,c=4$ and $d=-2$, which implies that \n\n$$\nad+bc=2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 4=16.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152598 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83c436d7-43de-5fc3-8ce9-ffee3522b4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150096} {:answer/id #uuid "878ee604-c103-5053-accd-021c977abe86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150097} {:answer/id #uuid "36a1f7e7-07d8-5e7b-b2d8-10439e7fbca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150098} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2f32a0-d9c2-5fff-92ef-17aaeb98ad1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150099} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddd25dc-12e2-58d9-ad7b-7e3c37c2d227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150100}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2e2f3bae-5cbf-5593-a8d7-5b3a83d8175d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150095}] :question/id #uuid "9b11f59e-fd24-5b44-aac3-13bb2025249f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38396" :question/problem "If $Re(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}$ and $Im(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $x = \\begin{bmatrix}3 - 5\\textrm{i} \\\\ 6 - 3\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of $ab + cd$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "603519cf-8fb2-5c1e-91e9-97ae1f25a1c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263832} {:answer/id #uuid "73c0fb30-a7bf-5234-ad98-c33dfcd17594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264006} {:answer/id #uuid "95c3dd1a-8eef-5d6f-b235-9b4ef128fe21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264284} {:answer/id #uuid "bab149df-5cb1-5f9a-a638-5b6a8d1b53b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264620} {:answer/id #uuid "c653dc48-3ab7-5c3d-9914-a9533d1e8131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264006} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f72e28c-749d-5aad-9d5d-25a4e600fe86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265364}] :question/id #uuid "96cc0784-cabd-554d-ad2d-61ea16cd06f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130890" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ then what is the value of $ac+bd?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=1,b=-1,c=-3$ and $d=-5$, which implies that \n\n$$\nac+bd=1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-5)=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa1ffbd-3480-51e5-a66d-959817fd10c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263364} {:answer/id #uuid "330ab03a-eba0-538e-b32c-dd738ce3c0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263439} {:answer/id #uuid "94ecc9aa-670f-5815-89c6-d055647572ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264275} {:answer/id #uuid "ee84c9b1-7eca-5cdb-afc6-6af4155fedfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265086} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e13ea5-33b0-5f5c-8464-f33818b2da1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265086} :answer-field/id #uuid "32e7aae1-2998-5d92-a004-1782963695ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265337}] :question/id #uuid "097ab3fa-0ddd-5641-9cb0-0d424e200e1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130891" :question/problem "Find the real and imaginary parts of the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}+2 \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}+2 \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdc00c7-d8aa-5cc7-a0a7-e8061f0c4597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342343} {:answer/id #uuid "370e629d-7450-5b57-a85f-8d0196bbea84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342692} {:answer/id #uuid "991b4be2-9c07-5193-b9aa-4ecfd119febb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343585} {:answer/id #uuid "b10a38b7-2940-5261-b192-a090479c92f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343792} {:answer/id #uuid "f16a7dda-c6e6-5eb7-97f3-4d5ae4e06145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342343} :answer-field/id #uuid "891badce-42b8-5f0c-8f29-af634cd7ba5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344733}] :question/id #uuid "6a3b677a-08b2-5263-b320-cb9f44b6bd97" :question/math-academy-id "q-76048" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}8+\\text{i} \\\\ -5+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ then what is the value of $ac-bd?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 6-3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}8+\\text{i} \\\\ -5+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=8,b=-5,c=1$ and $d=3$, which implies that \n\n$$\nac-bd=8\\cdot 1-(-5)\\cdot 3=23.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553516c6-59b1-5780-8471-747f180e0d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342945} {:answer/id #uuid "755a3198-13b4-5153-9d82-f2f5ee5fb5e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343252} {:answer/id #uuid "7c70f038-edf2-5c0e-aa32-20250dd8a3ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343309} {:answer/id #uuid "b87729bc-9a23-54e7-9c7b-45422cb90f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343858} {:answer/id #uuid "fc84d2d8-38ee-5707-84d6-a40d30a7e724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344459} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef807deb-e2ae-5391-aa19-1fcef30016bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344908}] :question/id #uuid "52941a01-ea01-5908-9173-c9bb5ba6d39c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76049" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ then what is the value of $bc-ad?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=-4,b=1,c=9$ and $d=8$, which implies that \n\n$$\nbc-ad=1\\cdot 9-(-4)\\cdot 8=41.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bbb921d-f6f4-5480-bfbf-c6d90fe64647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342862} {:answer/id #uuid "50b5dc8d-7e77-5191-97c8-29fe680f3d1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342906} {:answer/id #uuid "92681936-d9cd-5044-b0fa-03426cefa6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343516} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e79586-dfc4-5a38-b455-7f21a76e52eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344110} {:answer/id #uuid "f73494d8-9f5d-5cac-850f-97428a0e3f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344110} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2ed79a-afc0-55dd-b367-a5beca302e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344693}] :question/id #uuid "092a46e1-ab30-51e7-8a06-0f91ed1c7242" :question/math-academy-id "q-76050" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+bc?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=-6,b=1,c=7$ and $d=-6$, which implies that \n\n$$\nad+bc=(-6)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot 7=43.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406dbc4a-e01a-5357-9b25-3e8fa07a3099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342769} {:answer/id #uuid "a726f01a-8105-5643-a890-6bb474e773ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343709} {:answer/id #uuid "af1ac8b1-e1d6-5550-93a2-33a03b62c5a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343778} {:answer/id #uuid "d33b19d8-5839-51d0-b3bf-10f8a808ef87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344091} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f22006-2d95-5c53-8c67-1fb2daff5cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Im}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\," :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343709} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a9d7f5-d315-5a53-8cde-c10af7c42c07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344606}] :question/id #uuid "ad4a8de6-1917-5de3-bf8b-9b85c988593f" :question/math-academy-id "q-76052" :question/problem "Find the imaginary part of the vector $u=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i}+5 \\\\ -8\\text{i}+7\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,u=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i}+5 \\\\ -8\\text{i}+7\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i}+5 \\\\ -8\\text{i}+7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-8\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(u)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(u)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c8127b-dc32-5d32-b6c5-1d8268cbbaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} {:answer/id #uuid "1a447493-95b4-5171-9c27-c8d173b28036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342465} {:answer/id #uuid "4689eef9-d893-5fd3-ab4c-d948213d9844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342820} {:answer/id #uuid "6f976300-b408-5998-81f3-d99f702fa355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343198} {:answer/id #uuid "e9453c21-0e8a-5b5a-b3d0-e5f810eb92d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\text{Re}(v)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} :answer-field/id #uuid "716450b5-6a2d-560b-9d2e-23518d3edae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344697}] :question/id #uuid "07da44c0-ec24-5a2d-94d4-9974eaf9fe8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76053" :question/problem "Find the real part of the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\text{i}-4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\text{i}-4\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7\\text{i}-4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3+0\\text{i} \\\\ -4+7\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}\\,{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152206 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152016 :question/id #uuid "5ec4fe6e-b357-5721-86d0-298df3fd33cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-7345" :question/problem "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that \n![](images/8c/8c8e19d20f1b580e66eeb558341b4544d2785eb27ab602db7a221a6d9d80eefc.png)\nand\n![](images/2d/2d9551b937b1e8be3c56db51ca26943e1436e07acebc1bfb0f89c16e5e7dcafc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k}  = 8\\textrm{i}-12\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b1c3ace-b4ee-5b77-b91a-166f5f76d833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151542} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a20bd5-2716-5f04-a81e-063a924e5384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151543} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c187e6-f4c3-5b2f-bffc-5bf1f43dff98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151544} {:answer/id 